            <div xml:id="d489">

                <pb facs="0538" n="440" sameAs="frus:frus1930v02/pg440"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.003/349: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Johnson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peiping</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1930-05-08T14:00:00+08:00">May 8, 1930—2 p.m.</date><lb/>[Received
                        May 8—10:10 a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>316. Legation’s 304, May 3, 2 p.m. Following from the Minister: <quote
                        rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“British Minister showed Shigemitsu<anchor n="28" xml:id="d489-f1"/>
                            draft. He has now asked me for copy, and I am having copy of redraft
                            made to give to him although I suggested that his Foreign Office obtain
                            one by inquiry at Washington.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <closer>For the Minister:<lb/><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                        >Perkins</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d489-f1" n="28" xml:id="d489-f1-content">
                <p>Japanese Chargé in China.</p>
            </note>
